00:11:05.328 --> 00:11:10.568
a tape like this one, you expect the Bank of Canada to ease hard, yet the joint statement

00:11:10.568 --> 00:11:15.968
on the Bank of Canada site keeps the 2% target and the 1% to 3% control range in place.

00:11:15.968 --> 00:11:30.728
The bank strengthened its analysis of how global supply shocks transmit into Canadian inflation and will apply those lessons while staying inside the existing inflation targeting mandate, which is a change in homework, not a change in the reaction function.

00:11:31.308 --> 00:11:45.088
A credible, well-understood framework cuts uncertainty for households and businesses and supports investment and job creation even after repeated shocks, which is why the government of Canada and the bank review and renew that framework every five years.

00:11:45.088 --> 00:11:49.408
and then leave the bank to run policy independently against the agreed goals.

00:11:50.108 --> 00:11:55.108
Over the past five years, the framework took supply chain disruptions, rapid demand shifts,

00:11:55.668 --> 00:11:58.868
and geopolitical conflicts that pushed inflation higher worldwide,

00:11:59.388 --> 00:12:05.408
and the bank responded forcefully, bringing inflation back to the 2% target and inside the control range,

00:12:05.808 --> 00:12:09.528
which is evidence the framework itself held when implementation was ugly.

00:12:10.188 --> 00:12:14.088
The renewed statement underlines that high inflation erodes purchasing power

00:12:14.088 --> 00:12:19.608
and perceptions of fairness, which is the case for keeping inflation low, stable, and predictable,

00:12:20.128 --> 00:12:23.648
rather than treating every scare as a signal to rewrite the rulebook.

00:12:24.088 --> 00:12:28.788
Governor Tiff Macklem and senior deputy governor Carolyn Rogers appeared before the

00:12:28.788 --> 00:12:34.448
Standing Senate Committee on Banking, Commerce, and the Economy on November 5th, 2026,

00:12:34.968 --> 00:12:39.848
with the opening statement published at 1030 Eastern and no media availability afterward.

00:12:39.848 --> 00:12:44.868
And a useful habit is to read that opening statement the morning of any parliamentary appearance,

00:12:45.208 --> 00:12:49.848
so you can map the exact supply-side language onto your holdings before the tape does it

00:12:49.848 --> 00:12:50.268
for you.

00:12:50.828 --> 00:12:55.588
The common mis is assuming every economic shock automatically triggers a policy shift.

00:12:56.068 --> 00:13:00.828
The fix is to treat the framework renewal as the anchor and only move a rate-sensitive position

00:13:01.128 --> 00:13:03.868
when the bank signals a change in its reaction function.

00:13:04.448 --> 00:13:07.288
Remember, the framework is the anchor, not the shock.

